// Loop runs and rollouts (#722), the API a trainer drives Loop environments
// through.
//
// A person mints a run when they connect a trainer. It pins one published
// environment version and, optionally, one task dataset version, and holds the
// run's limits. The trainer then resets rollouts in it, steps each with tool
// calls, and closes it; a rollout's rewards come from its verifier VM at
// close, never from the environment it ran in. A GRPO group is the rollouts of
// one task reset together, each restored from the same snapshot.
//
// A machine credential with the `rollout:drive` scope may call
// ResetLoopRollout, StepLoopRollout, CloseLoopRollout, ForkLoopRollout,
// GetLoopRun and GetLoopRollout; every other RPC is a person's. A refusal
// carries LoopRolloutRejectionV1 and a stable code. Failures on our side are
// never billed.
//
// Same package as evaluation.proto, in its own FILE as environment.proto is. A
// later change adds fields; it never renames one.

